WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:01.180
<b>Express to the Main Island
of Enies Lobby</b>

3
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.620
[LUCCI]
It's been quite a while, Chief.

4
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.800
Hasn't it?

5
00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:17.880
[LUCCI]
As promised, we've brought Cutty Flam...
the criminal responsible for assaulting

6
00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.080
government officials in
Water Seven, 8 years ago.

7
00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.080
And of course.

8
00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.990
We also have Nico Robin,
the last surviving resident of Ohara.

9
00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:29.130
Who we've been trying to capture
for the past two decades.

10
00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.890
They're both waiting outside
if you would like to see them.

11
00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.740
In short, the mission
was a huge success.

12
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.010
[SPANDAM]
It's good to have you back.

13
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:38.910
Lucci.

14
00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:39.800
Kaku.

15
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.760
Blueno.

16
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.930
Kalifa.

17
00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:42.870
[KALIFA]
That's harassment.

18
00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.900
[SPANDAM]
All I did was say your name!

19
00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.710
[JABURA]
Just like old times, huh, Lucci?

20
00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:55.000
Actually, I think that you might
be even more smug than before.

21
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.140
But sadly, you're
not any smarter, Jabra.

22
00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.570
[JABURA]
What?

23
00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.510
[KAKU]
Oh, come on!

24
00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.570
We've hardly even
gotten off of the train

25
00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.010
and the first thing you
two do is start bickering?

26
00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:06.910
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi!

27
00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.780
[KUMADORI]
Kaakuu is riiiiight!

28
00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:13.380
Can't we alllll just get aloooong?!

29
00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:20.790
Fooor fiiive loooong years we've
awaaaaited theiiir reeetuuurn!

30
00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.360
[FUKURO]
Chapapa.

31
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.520
Ow.

32
00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.820
[KALIFA]
I had a feeling you were going
to test us right away, Fukurou.

33
00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:49.390
[FUKURO]
Six Powers Skill-Competition!

34
00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.290
I'll use an armed guard as
reference for the ranking.

35
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.840
<b>Power Level 10</b>

36
00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.900
Let's say they're about a ten.

37
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.360
So your power levels are.

38
00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.230
Ohhh, interesting, very interesting.

39
00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.370
Let's see here.

40
00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:01.530
First is Kalifa.

41
00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.500
Power level six hundred thirty.

42
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.830
Blueno is eight-hundred twenty.

43
00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.140
Kaku is two-thousand, two hundred.

44
00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.240
And Lucci.

45
00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.200
Power level 4000!

46
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.340
[JABURA]
4000?

47
00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.150
You gotta be making these numbers up!

48
00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.290
There's no such thing as
a power level that high!

49
00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.750
Cha pa pa!

50
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:28.230
Well, maybe not before now,
but they've gotten stronger!

51
00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.830
Since I measured
Jabra and Kumadori too.

52
00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:35.130
I can finally rank all of CP9!

53
00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:41.600
[JABURA]
No way, Fukurou, I want a recount!

54
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.310
Even if I ignore the whole Lucci thing,
why the hell am I weaker than Kaku!

55
00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:46.780
'Because Cha pa pa!

56
00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:50.350
Kaku got stronger too, that's why!

57
00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.710
[JABURA]
I don't want you getting
a big head over this Kaku.

58
00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.170
Just remember, the "Competition" technique
only measures your physical strength!

59
00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.020
In a real battle,

60
00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.500
I have my devil fruit powers
to help me out, too.

61
00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.660
I can trash a guy like you
any day of the week, got it?

62
00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.860
[KAKU]
I don't care.

63
00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.100
If it makes you feel better,
keep telling yourself that.

64
00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.240
Exactly.

65
00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.040
Don't pay any heed to the
yapping of that mangy dog.

66
00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:16.910
So, I'm a mangy dog, am I?

67
00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.810
Screw you, cat bastard.

68
00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:27.910
[KALIFA]
Honestly!

69
00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.580
Both of you, stop it!

70
00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.310
Jabra certainly is
touchy today, isn't he?

71
00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.880
Did something happen to him?

72
00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.550
All the guards on the
island are talking about it!

73
00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.550
Jabra's been in a bad mood
'cause he got dumped

74
00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.850
by that waitress,
Gatherine the other day.

75
00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:43.190
[BLUENO]
So that's it.

76
00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.820
[JABURA]
Hey, now hold on a sec!

77
00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.070
That's a secret-why do
people know about that!

78
00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.140
'Cause I told everyone here
how sad and lonely you are!

79
00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:51.070
Chapapa!

80
00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:53.780
I should've known!

81
00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.880
<b>Gatherine</b>

82
00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.330
[SPANDAM]
Geez!

83
00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.440
This is what you get for doing that
stupid ranking nonsense right off the bat!

84
00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.040
There's hardly any point in bickering

85
00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.840
over who's strongest when your Six Powers
training has made you all superhuman.

86
00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.380
Power Level 500 should be
more than anyone needs, right?

87
00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.350
He's saying that cause he's level 9.

88
00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.750
Even weaker than a guard, chapapa!

89
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:18.820
Who cares!

90
00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:21.190
You guys are the muscle...I
just give the orders!

91
00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.060
Besides, I have my special
sword to use in a pinch.

92
00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:24.930
[KALIFA]
It's all right, Chief.

93
00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.160
We've always known how weak you are.

94
00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.230
[SPANDAM]
Come on now, Kalifa.

95
00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:33.330
There's no need to
be so blunt about it!

96
00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.670
[KALIFA]
That's sexual harassment.

97
00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.370
[SPANDAM]
What?

98
00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.900
Because I replied to you?

99
00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.570
[SPANDAM]
By the way.

100
00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:40.220
Huh?

101
00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:40.920
What now?

102
00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.150
[KALIFA]
That's sexual harassment.

103
00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:44.690
My existence?

104
00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.340
Yoiyoi!

105
00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.380
Kalifa!

106
00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:51.000
You are showing very poor form!

107
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.790
Allow me to apologiiize,
deaaar chiiief.

108
00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.790
By putting this blade to my belly!

109
00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.290
Seppuku!

110
00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.790
[KUMADORI]
Iron Body!

111
00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.300
I can't even die right.

112
00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:08.080
[JABURA]
If you wanna die that bad,
I'd be happy to help!

113
00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.830
Although it's been a long time
coming, needless to say,

114
00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:15.380
Needless to say, I'm extremely pleased
with your performance in this mission.

115
00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:18.790
By the way, although it
isn't exactly a reward for all

116
00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.360
your hard work, I do have
something I want to give you.

117
00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.730
But we can take care of that later.

118
00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:29.360
For now, let's meet them, shall we?

119
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.890
The hope of the entire world.

120
00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:43.940
[OFFICIAL]
Hurry up!

121
00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:45.740
Move it!

122
00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.050
[OFFICIAL]
You too, big guy!

123
00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.420
[SPANDAM]
I couldn't be happier!

124
00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:04.620
Amazing work.

125
00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:10.160
You survived the "accident"
eight years ago, Cutty Flam.

126
00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:13.230
And now, I have you as well.

127
00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:17.400
The world's most dangerous
woman, Nico Robin.

128
00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.390
It's so unfortunate.

129
00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.490
The rest of the world may never know

130
00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:24.320
what a glorious accomplishment
CP9 achieved today.

131
00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:27.590
One of the drawbacks of being
a secret agency and all that.

132
00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.000
Yes, a pity.

133
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.590
Honestly, the news of your capture
could take years to reach the public.

134
00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.090
The "justice" those old geezers

135
00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:40.890
in the current World Government
dole out is far too lenient!

136
00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:44.810
Without sacrifice,
goals cannot be achieved.

137
00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:49.940
I mean, this is world peace we're
working for... it's not easy!

138
00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:52.350
Surely there can't be
an issue with sacrificing

139
00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:56.460
a few fools along the way who hinder our
work for the sake of the greater good.

140
00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:57.390
Right?

141
00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.460
You know, if everyone
would just give us

142
00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:01.700
what we ask for obediently
and without question.

143
00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.400
Then we wouldn't need to
go to such extreme measures.

144
00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.170
Like we had to with poor Tom!

145
00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.360
That traitor deserved it!

146
00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.560
[FRANKY]
Crazy bastard!

147
00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.130
[FRANKY]
Tom put his life on the line
to protect those blueprints!

148
00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:22.000
Because idiots like you exist!

149
00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:27.350
[SPANDAM]
What are you doing?!

150
00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.910
Don't just sit there, help me!

151
00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.390
[SPANDAM]
Kumadoriii!

152
00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:43.980
[KUMADORI]
Yoyoi! What is your desiiiiiiire?

153
00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.770
[SPANDAM]
Isn't it obvious?! Help me! Make him stop!

154
00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.900
[KUMADORI]
Saa. Saa. Saa!

155
00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:14.010
[LUFFY]
Now Gum-Gum Gatling!

156
00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.810
Now Gum-Gum Whip!

157
00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.930
Giant Sickle!

158
00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:25.770
Bell!

159
00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.150
Hammer!

160
00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.780
Bazooka!

161
00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.910
Gum-Gum Stamp!

162
00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.390
[MARINE]
This is Main Island, calling the Chief.

163
00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.790
Spandam, come in!

164
00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.460
I repeat! Come in!

165
00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.360
[MARINE]
It's no good!

166
00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.460
No signal!

167
00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:52.360
Is that so?

168
00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.330
Maybe he's got the receiver off again.

169
00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:55.630
[MARINE]
Awww, seriously?!

170
00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.710
Could his timing be any worse?!

171
00:10:58.710 --> 00:10:59.410
[MARINE]
Hey!

172
00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.310
Anyone see where Straw Hat went?

173
00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:02.910
[MARINE]
He's right beneath you!

174
00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:03.780
[MARINE]
What?!

175
00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:04.880
He is?!

176
00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.550
[MARINE]
Everyone attack him from all sides!

177
00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:10.410
Now!

178
00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:11.080
[MARINE]
There he is!

179
00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:11.780
We got him!

180
00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:12.480
Damn!

181
00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.590
I'm cornered!

182
00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:26.030
[LUFFY]
Now Gum-Gum Volcano!

183
00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.050
[OFFICIAL]
What?!

184
00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:51.890
No way!

185
00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.420
The walls are falling!

186
00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:56.460
[OFFICIAL]
Run!

187
00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:05.570
[LUFFY]
Now Gum-Gum Gatling!

188
00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.510
[MARINE]
Oh, no!

189
00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:14.520
[MARINE]
Chief Spandam!

190
00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.590
Please, come in!

191
00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.050
We need your orders, sir!

192
00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.850
We can't stop Straw Hat Luffy!

193
00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:21.550
[MARINE]
Get ready!

194
00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:25.890
<b>Courthouse, Main Island
Enies Lobby</b>

195
00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.860
He's heading towards the courthouse!

196
00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.470
We need those defenses lined up!

197
00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:26.400
[MARINE]
Move it, men!

198
00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.940
[LEFT BASKERVILLE]
Shut up, already!

199
00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:29.400
[CENTER BASKERVILLE]
What's with all the yelling?

200
00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:32.270
[RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
You guys woke me up!

201
00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.070
[MARINE]
Chief Justice!

202
00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:37.690
<b>"Three-Headed" Baskerville
Chief Justice, Enies Lobby</b>

203
00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.020
[BASKERVILLE]
Yep!

204
00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.090
You got it!

205
00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:37.790
That's me!

206
00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.230
<b>"Three-Headed" Baskerville
Chief Justice, Enies Lobby</b>

207
00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.580
Chief Justice of Enies Lobby!

208
00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:41.840
[LEFT BASKERVILLE]
On the left!

209
00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:45.030
My name is Left Baskerville!

210
00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.330
[RIGHT BASKERVILLE]
On the right!

211
00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:49.200
I am Right Baskerville!

212
00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:54.350
[CENTER BASKERVILLE]
And, located in the center,
I am known as Central Freeway!

213
00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.400
[ALL THREE BASKERVILLES]
Say what?!

214
00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:56.430
[MARINE]
Chief Justice.

215
00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:56.350
Uh.

216
00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:58.360
We've got a problem.

217
00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:00.690
There's a pirate on a rampage
on the Main Island, sir.

218
00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:04.280
But we can't get in touch with Chief
Spandam to get an update on our orders.

219
00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.130
Please, sir, take
command on his behalf!

220
00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.600
A pirate, you say?

221
00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:11.300
All pirates are guilty!

222
00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.270
[CENTER BASKERVILLE]
There hasn't been a trial yet!

223
00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:17.630
Even so, I think he's innocent!

224
00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:18.330
[CENTER BASKERVILLE]
Then.

225
00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.030
I'll be neutral.

226
00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:20.830
Death!

227
00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:23.960
[ALL THREE BASKERVILLES]
Say what?!

228
00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:24.990
[MARINE]
Chief Justice!

229
00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.460
There's trouble, sir!

230
00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:27.630
I just received a report.

231
00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:31.010
The Straw Hat's accomplices have
taken out Kaahii at the Front Gate.

232
00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:33.010
Oimo's still fighting,
but won't last much longer!

233
00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:33.710
[BASKERVILLE]
Say what?!

234
00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:36.550
That gate must not be breached!

235
00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.880
Send one hundred Watchdogs
to that location immediately!

236
00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:46.720
[GUARDS]
Sir!

237
00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:49.350
<b>Island Gate
Enies Lobby</b>

238
00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.790
[FAMILY MAN]
We're in trouble!

239
00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.670
Our 5 minute window is up!

240
00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:50.370
Damn!

241
00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:51.110
Hurry!

242
00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:53.270
We've got to get that
gate open for Rocketman!

243
00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.680
[OIMO]
I will never let you through!

244
00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:57.830
[MOZU]
Okay guys!

245
00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:58.700
We picked the gate's lock!

246
00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:01.540
[KIWI]
All you have to do now is push it open!

247
00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.240
[OIMO]
What?!

248
00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:02.940
Oh, crap!

249
00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:03.650
[FAMILY MAN]
Nice work!

250
00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:04.350
You heard her!

251
00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.510
[FAMILY MAN]
Move it!

252
00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:09.720
You stay away from that gate!

253
00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.460
[PAULIE]
Rope Action!

254
00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:13.890
[PAULIE]
Top Knot!

255
00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:18.390
Whoa!

256
00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:20.260
[FAMILY MAN]
Those Galley-La foremen are incredible!

257
00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:23.560
You think this puny
rope is gonna hold me?!

258
00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.890
Franky Family!

259
00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:26.760
Pull!

260
00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.320
[FAMILY MEN]
Yeah!

261
00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.290
No problem!

262
00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:30.630
Gomorrah!

263
00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:31.330
Sodom!

264
00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:32.960
Grab that rope!

265
00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:39.780
[FAMILY MAN]
Move it, Franky Family!

266
00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:43.200
Don't stop until that
gate is wide open!

267
00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.640
[OIMO]
Oi, oi, oi!

268
00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:45.540
Hold on!

269
00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:46.340
Slow down!

270
00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:47.640
I'm getting dizzy!

271
00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.480
[FAMILY MAN]
Push the gate!

272
00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:55.490
[MARINE]
No!

273
00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:56.560
Impossible!

274
00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.290
The gates are opening!

275
00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.880
[MARINE]
What the hell is Oimo doing?!

276
00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:02.550
A little more.

277
00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.560
[MARINE]
They've breached the gate!

278
00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.850
<b>Main Gate</b>

279
00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.740
[OFFICIAL]
Hey! Hey!

280
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.510
[MARINE]
There's no way.

281
00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:34.840
Is that a sea train?

282
00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:36.140
What's going on here?

283
00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.160
It is!

284
00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:51.820
Look at it!

285
00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:52.530
A sea train!

286
00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:53.730
And it's not the Puffing Tom!

287
00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:57.460
It's another one, and it's
headed this way at full speed!

288
00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:58.430
[MARINE]
They're crazy!

289
00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.970
What're they trying
to do...jump the fence?

290
00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.050
[OFFICIAL]
Hurry!

291
00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:04.750
Close the gate!

292
00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.020
We can't let them through!

293
00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:07.720
[OFFICIAL]
Come on!

294
00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:08.980
Get those doors shut!

295
00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.080
[ZORO]
Hey, granny!

296
00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:20.930
[KOKORO]
Yeah? What is it?

297
00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:24.060
I need you to give me as much
speed as you've got, okay?

298
00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:26.370
[KOKORO]
It seems we've had to
switch up our plans a little.

299
00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:30.370
Your green-haired samurai friend says you
all should find something to hold onto.

300
00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.060
[NAMI]
Find something to hold on to

301
00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.480
[SANJI]
Hey, Moss-for-Brains!

302
00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:35.730
What's going on out here?

303
00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:38.860
[ZORO]
They, uh, they closed the Main Gate.

304
00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:40.250
[SOGEKING]
They what?!

305
00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.090
This is bad!

306
00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:42.900
We're gonna crash!

307
00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:44.400
[CHOPPER]
What are we gonna do?!
What are we gonna do?!

308
00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:48.440
Dodge it, Kokoro!

309
00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.270
I've got a plan.

310
00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:51.340
Don't worry.

311
00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:57.080
Hey, Frog!

312
00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:57.680
See fence?

313
00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:58.410
Smash!

314
00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.750
[ALL THREE]
What?!

315
00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.520
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

316
00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.420
Gero, Gero!

317
00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:16.730
Gero, Gero, Gero, Gero!

318
00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:26.380
[KOKORO]
That's his plan?!

319
00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.110
Does he realize what's gonna happen
when we run into that fence?!

320
00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:42.540
[OFFICIAL]
Impossible!

321
00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:43.480
That seatrain!

322
00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:45.710
[MARINE]
It's flying!

323
00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:47.620
[SOGEKING]
No!

324
00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.090
We're gonna die!

325
00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:49.930
What?!

326
00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.960
But I don't wanna die!

327
00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.600
[SANJI]
Nami! This way! I'll
save you! Fall into my arms!

328
00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:56.430
[NAMI]
Shut up, you idiot!

329
00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:58.770
I've got enough problems right now!

330
00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.270
[NAMI]
Zoro!

331
00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:09.450
You'd better have thought long and hard
about how you're gonna land this thing!

332
00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.880
Of course I have!

333
00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:20.090
We fall.

334
00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:20.960
[YOKOZUNA]
Gero!

335
00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.590
[EVERYONE]
I hate you!

336
00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:26.220
We'll find out if luck's
on our side soon enough.

337
00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.600
[MARINE]
Oimo's going down!

338
00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:50.820
[OFFICIAL]
Whoa!

339
00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:51.790
What a crew!

340
00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:53.260
Are you Straw Hats?

341
00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.260
[KIWI & MOZU]
Damn straight!

342
00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:56.740
Is that so?!

343
00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:57.810
That doesn't matter.

344
00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.710
Let's move. Time's a' wasting.

345
00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:00.910
We've gotta clear a path.

346
00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.780
And fast.

347
00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:02.480
All right!

348
00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.750
You heard him, guys!

349
00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.180
We need to go deeper!

350
00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:06.680
Let's make a hole!

351
00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:09.020
[FAMILY MEN]
Yeah!

352
00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:23.910
[LULU]
Paulie! No!

353
00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.850
[PAULIE]
Who in the hell are you?

354
00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:26.880
Who, us?

355
00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:27.980
I'll tell you.

356
00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:30.650
The First-Class Guards of Enies Lobby.

357
00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:33.390
The Watchdogs of the Law.

358
00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:36.030
<b>Watchdogs of the Law
Elite Guards of Enies Lobby</b>

359
00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:36.240
By order of Chief Justice Baskerville.

360
00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:39.770
For your crimes,
you're sentenced to death!

361
00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:41.250
Damn.

362
00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:42.850
They just keep coming!

363
00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:44.150
One after another.

364
00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.090
[WATCHDOG CAPTAIN]
Oimo!

365
00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:46.380
What are you doing?

366
00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:48.850
How could you let this pirate
riff-raff open the gate?

367
00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.120
What's wrong with you?

368
00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.700
Can't believe I passed out!

369
00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:02.610
[KIWI & MOZU]
That giant's back up and on his feet!

370
00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:58.940
Oh crap!

371
00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.240
[OIMO]
Little jerks!

372
00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.950
You're dead!

373
00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:07.650
You'll pay!

374
00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:08.350
Whoa!

375
00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:35.590
What the...?!

376
00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:38.060
Rocketman fell from the sky!

377
00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:41.000
[ALL FOUR]
We opened those gates for nothing?!

378
00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:50.800
Huh?!

379
00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:52.100
What the hell just happened?

380
00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.070
Man, that was some landing!

381
00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:56.700
Do you think that they're okay?

382
00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:04.440
They're not coming out.

383
00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:21.640
[MARINE]
Hey! You guys all right?

384
00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:25.940
[OFFICIAL]
What?!

385
00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:26.870
Impossible!

386
00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:28.680
Who are those two?

387
00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:39.670
Huh... Maybe we should have
introduced ourselves first.

388
00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:40.540
[SANJI]
Nah.

389
00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.240
I'd rather let my feet do the talking.

390
00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:44.110
[KIWI & MOZU]
The Straw Hats are here!

391
00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:47.910
We've been waiting for you!

392
00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:50.390
[ZORO]
Excellent.

393
00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:53.980
Just like I planned it.

394
00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:54.680
Whoa!

395
00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.780
Really?!
